al SCC contains such ties remains open.',['S_exec'],['B_apply'])]\ndef path(ex,bs,fs,ss):return dict(explanation=ex,behavior_ids=bs,fact_ids=fs,source_ids=ss)\nM=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go EPaxos package with shared replica transport, master registration, configuration entry and command State. Other protocols named by README/run.go are outside this investigation.',protocol_contexts=[ctx,'Default run: static configured peers; F=(configured replicas-1)/2; crash failures described by runReplica; durable=false, thriftiness=true, LRead=false, Dreply=true.'],external_interfaces=['Client PROPOSE byte stream','Replica typed RPC stream over TCP','Master Register/Ping/BeTheLeader net/rpc'],ownership=['Protocol run serializes message handlers. Separate execution goroutine consumes shared InstanceSpace; network listeners decode and enqueue RPCs.'],selection_injection=['Constructors accept peer list, failures and execution flags; in-repository runReplica supplies defaults.'],variants=['N<=3 thrifty equality special case','N>7 committed-dependency condition','Optional durability, batching, transconf and beacon adaptation'],source_ids=['S_run','S_init','S_members','S_dispatch','S_profile'],unknowns=['No crash-restart reconstruction or dynamic membership contract established.']),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=surfaces,core_overview=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation and authority paths, caller/transport boundaries and application/recovery support have been read. Usable navigation does not validate the observed thresholds, state transitions or transport semantics.',formation=path('Client proposals allocate an origin-row instance and preaccept with dependency/sequence attributes from conflict indexes. Acceptor preaccept reports are filtered by the coordinator attempt and phase; replies merge attributes. The configured fast threshold with equality/commit-prefix/initial-ballot conditions commits; otherwise an Accept phase uses acceptOKs+1>N/2. Commit broadcasts full commands and dependencies; receivers install only when not already committed and not below their promise. Execution waits for dependency availability/commitment, traverses SCCs, executes and responds through retained client proposals. Actual formulas and absent status changes are observations requiring validation, not assertions of quorum sufficiency.',['B_client','B_phase1','B_form','B_accept','B_commit','B_apply'],['F_local_value','F_decision'],['S_phase1','S_pa_reply','S_accept','S_commit','S_members','S_exec']),context=path('Authority is scoped to origin-row/instance and ballot, not one global log leader. startRecovery replaces bookkeeping, retains proposals, chooses an attempt ballot, retags its local entry and includes a self report before Prepare broadcast. Remote Prepare raises only the promise bal and reports vbal separately. Coordinator accepts matching-attempt replies while preparing, waits for SlowQuorumSize including self, selects by VBallot, then installs committed data, resumes Accept, or restarts phase1. Old requests below a local promise are dropped/reported without replacement; old reply ballots and finished phases are filtered. Same-ballot reuse and preservation of value tags through codecs are open local anomalies.',['B_authority','B_prepare_wire','B_recover_select'],['F_prepare_report','F_local_value'],['S_watch','S_recover_start','S_prepare','S_recover_select','S_prepare_codec']),connection=path('Recovery reports are the bridge from prior formation to authority transfer: promise Ballot qualifies the new attempt, while VBallot and Status decide which existing support the new coordinator uses. Commit/execute states constrain overwrite and skip ordinary recovery. Pending proposals survive bookkeeping replacement and may be requeued on own-row NOOP commit. The execution watcher can solicit recovery for missing/uncommitted known work; master selection only influences makeBallot through IsLeader. Wire decoding lies directly on the report path and must be investigated before treating reported value tags as preserved. No unread persistent recovery mechanism is assumed to repair it.',['B_authority','B_prepare_wire','B_recover_select','B_recovery_watch','B_commit','B_membership'],['F_prepare_report','F_local_value','F_decision'],['S_prepare','S_recover_select','S_recover_start','S_watch','S_commit','S_members','S_transport_recv']),open_details=['PrepareReply VBallot wire preservation is the first selected discriminator.','Accepted status retention, ballot reuse/retagging and quorum formula applicability remain separate leads.','Durable restart contract, SCAN dependency coverage, equal-sequence SCC ordering and full client retry policy remain unresolved.'],core_gaps=[]))\nq=dict(question='Does the registered PrepareReply transport preserve the producer-reported value ballot for a legally reached nonzero-vbal instance, as required for recovery to distinguish prior support, or does decoding replace that context before handlePrepareReply selects metadata?',importance='Recovery uses VBallot to select prior command/dependency/status support. Losing that context could alter recovery selection and threaten decision preservation; no cluster safety violation is established.',source_ids=['S_prepare','S_prepare_codec','S_reply_type','S_recover_select','S_transport_send','S_transport_recv','S_rpc','S_phase1','S_pa_codec'],participants=['Acceptor reporting instance state','Recovery coordinator receiving PrepareReply'],objects=['PrepareReply','Instance','LeaderBookkeeping.prepareReplies'],contexts=['Nonzero original or later value ballot; intact in-memory state; default thrifty crash-stop configuration','Typed RPC creation through PrepareReply.New and current codecs'],event_paths=['startPhase1 or handlePreAccept establishes vbal -> handlePrepare raises bal and constructs report -> replyPrepare/SendMsg/Marshal -> New/Unmarshal -> handlePrepareReply reads VBallot'],activit